            <ArticleTitle>An unusual presentation of genitourinary schistosomiasis in a Caucasian woman in the UK.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young woman who presented with loin pain and pyuria after a prolonged period of investigations and treatment, finally having a nephrectomy for non-functioning kidney, was revealed to have schistosomial infestation with an adult worm in the ureter. Unusually, she only developed bladder manifestations later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
